{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1154628-recommend-me-some-w20-books","id":1154628,"title":"Recommend me some W20 books?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-31T22:44:31-07:00","id":1154628,"title":"Recommend me some W20 books?","content":"So, I have the W20 Core, Changing Breeds, and Kinfolk books, and was wondering what other W20 books are around now, and which ones I should certainly look into picking up? How is Book of the Wyrm 20 for example? What W20 books are considered the best of the bunch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1069-archmage-joda","name":"Archmage Joda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:18:29-07:00","id":1154797,"title":"","content":"Well W20 Book of the Wyrm is a work of twisted beauty and W20 Umbra is also very good. W20 Rage Across the World is nice for a few extra Totems, Gifts, Fetishes and info about places etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T13:09:49-07:00","id":1154817,"title":"","content":"The book of the wyrm is quite good IMHO, gave me a lot of ideas about potential plots and scenes; I'd advise against it only if you don't like involving the Pentex in your campaigns, since it's half of the book. Umbra: the Velvet Shadow details the near Umbra reams and you may need it if you don't own the Revised Umbra of the 2nd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T13:18:27-07:00","id":1154821,"title":"","content":"Book of the Wyrm 20, is my second favorite book released by Onyx Path(Hunters Hunted 2 is first). <br /> <br /> Highly recommend it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T20:10:52-07:00","id":1154950,"title":"","content":"I don't think any of the books out there are bad but you get more bang for your buck from Umbra and Wyrm since they have the most generic uses in different sorts of games. Rage across the world is a well done book with some nice new bits, BUT unless you are going to be doing a world traveling chronicle it has its limits.<br /> <br /> Shattered Dreams, Wyld West update, Tribebook White Howlers are all neat but really are setups for particular alternative setting games.<br /> <br /> The Werewolf cookbook doesn't help at all unless you want to cook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T14:28:24-08:00","id":1157361,"title":"","content":"If you have interest in a particular tribe, consider buying the revised edition &quot;tribe book&quot; for them. In addition to a richer flavor of the tribe's culture and values, you'll find some really good short stories in them, such as &quot;The Weakness of Uli Brightjaws&quot; in the Get of Fenris book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T02:29:02-08:00","id":1157724,"title":"","content":"I'd say it depends on what your focus will be;<br /> <br /> Kinfolk 20th, if you want to focus on the mundane experiences between garou and their kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Umbra 20th, if your focus is on spiritual things in general. Umbra is great, because it makes the spirits ACTUAL characters and not just plot devices.<br /> <br /> Rage Across the World, if you want to focus on non-American settings or if you want a general look on the World in WtA.<br /> <br /> Wyrm 20th, if you want to dig deeper into the Wyrm-lore and turn BSDs from pictish madmen into something akin to the Boltons for GoT.<br /> <br /> Shattered Dreams, if you wish to explore the atrocities Garou have committed over the centuries.<br /> <br /> Skinner SAS, if you'd like to use Skindancers as bad guys in your story.<br /> <br /> TB:White Howlers, if you want to see how the fallen tribe lived in your story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}